*        ICM condition code must follow the LEFTMOST inserted byte, not the
*        first inserted byte with a high bit set. Mask 1100 selects the two
*        high-order bytes; the leftmost byte is 0x01 (high bit clear) and the
*        second is 0x80 (high bit set). The correct code is 2, not 1.
         ORG   0x1000
START    BALR  12,0
         USING *,12
         ICM   1,0xC,SRC
         DIAG  0,0,0
SRC      DC    X'0180'
         END   START
